ategory_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"ZfzTw5exIOalHsGlK99y-w","review_id":"ew3kRwZc9uBoKIM96_4l9Q","date":"2018-01-02T20:31:09","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9445371031761169,"text_excerpt":"Almost hidden in a quiet, industrial area in New Orleans East is a gem of a brewery. The place is HUGE, but they've made the bar feel intimate and friendly. There have been a lot of brew pubs popping up, this one is worth the drive. We tried the \"big-kid\" flight (half-pints of each beer), of their beers: Culicidae Ale - Excellent staple beer. Easy to drink, good sports watching beer. The more you drink, the less able you are to pronounce the name. Fruit Fly ASB American Special Bitter Ale - Loved this one because the brew master \"made up\" the ASB designation. He figured if there's an \"ESB (English)\", there should be an American version. Bug Leight Session Steam Lager - I'm not much of a l..."},{"business_id":"ZfzTw5exIOalHsGlK99y-w","review_id":"SxzloRrsymyu3F6bJ7JFWQ","date":"2017-06-12T17:30:11","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9316130876541138,"text_excerpt":"I really like what this place is about! Good beer done well. The inviting space is tucked away in an industrial section of New Orleans east. There is a large sign pointing you to the brewery off Townsend place since many of the warehouses look the same. Picnic tables are available in the front and on the side. A small bar area with half a dozen stools, a large rope spool for a standing table and a \"kids room\" make this a fun spot. The space is huge and will easily accommodate a crowd. When you enter you're likely to be greeted by Ray, Michael or Mandy. They have set up a nice brewery that is planned for growth. If you spend a few minutes with any of them you immediately know they are abou..."},{"business_id":"ZfzTw5exIOalHsGlK99y-w","review_id":"Dj4QWtflf6IddEbVop90Yg","date":"2017-06-11T00:11:29","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9249600768089294,"text_excerpt":"I thoroughly enjoyed my afternoon at Royal Brewery and I have the tshirt to prove it. Located in the Industry Hub, Lakefront South, Bywater North (branding is everything see eg Mid city formerly the 7th ward etc). Any way, located in New Orleans East, they are a much welcome change of pace. Currently they have two brews on tap and sometimes a non alcoholic homemade ginger ale option. Both brews are light and the head frothy almost like a foam on a latte. The ginger ale is super delicious and... not so strong that you clear your sinuses. When you stop by you will be treated like family. Many times there is food available and there is a kids section with activities. What what! There is limi..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"ZfzTw5exIOalHsGlK99y-w","photo_id":"-gUCdfuW25Ncuo1kvK-z2g","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/-gUCdfuW25Ncuo1kvK-z2g.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8844338655471802},{"business_id":"ZfzTw5exIOalHsGlK99y-w","photo_id":"hOYsRM14PBBkUgqteplo3Q","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/hOYsRM14PBBkUgqteplo3Q.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8844338059425354}]},"notebook_case":null}
